  "chapter": {
    "number": 2,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          "Now the Lord had commanded a great whale to swallow up Jonas: and Jonas was in the belly of the whale three days and three nights."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          "And Jonas prayed to the Lord his God out of the belly of the whale,"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          "and said, I cried in my affliction to the Lord my God, and he listened to me, even to my cry out of the belly of hell: you heard my voice."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          "You did cast me into the depths of the heart of the sea, and the floods compassed me: all your billows and your waves have passed upon me."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          "And I said, I am cast out of your presence: shall I indeed look again toward your holy temple?"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          "Water was poured around me to the soul: the",
          {
            "noteId": 5
          },
          "lowest deep compassed me, my head went down"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          "to the clefts of the mountains; I went down into the earth, whose bars are the everlasting barriers: yet, O Lord my God, let my ruined life be restored."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          "When my soul was failing",
          {
            "noteId": 6
          },
          "me, I remembered the Lord; and may my prayer come to you into your holy temple."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          "They that observe",
          {
            "noteId": 7
          },
          "vanities and lies have forsaken their own mercy."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          "But I will sacrifice to you with the voice of praise and thanksgiving: all that I have vowed I will pay to you,",
          {
            "noteId": 8
          },
          "the Lord of my salvation."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          "And the whale was commanded by the Lord, and it cast up Jonas on the dry land."
        ]
      }
    ],
